-- Where an @nlg herald shows on hover (smucclaw/l4-ide#979, ruled 2026-09-26).
-- Hover shows what `l4 nlg` and `l4 render` print, not where the herald sits.

-- Test 1: a herald written after the head's INPUT is the RULE's sentence.
-- Hovering the rule name shows it; hovering the input in the head does not.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`row five` amount @nlg row five saw %amount%
  MEANS amount GREATER THAN 100

-- Test 2: a herald written in the GIVEN is the input's gloss (smucclaw#977).
-- Hovering the input still shows it; the rule has no sentence of its own.
GIVEN total IS A NUMBER @nlg the sum of money
DECIDE `p seven` IF total GREATER THAN 200

-- Test 3: a call site of the rule from Test 1. The map is restamped only at
-- the definition, so hover here is unchanged by #979.
DECIDE `row five check` IS `row five` 200

-- Test 4 (control): a herald on its own line above the head is the rule's
-- sentence, and it was always stamped on the declaration, not moved by #979.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg the claim of %amount% is large
DECIDE `is large` IF amount GREATER THAN 100

-- Test 5 (control): a herald trailing the rule's name in its head.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is small` @nlg the claim of %amount% is small
  IF amount LESS THAN 10

-- Test 6 (control): a herald on a GIVEN type variable is that variable's gloss.
GIVEN a IS A TYPE @nlg the kind of thing
      x IS AN a
GIVETH AN a
`same thing` MEANS x

-- Test 7 (control for Test 3): call sites of Tests 4 and 5. A reference never
-- shows a herald on hover, wherever the herald was written.
DECIDE `large check` IS `is large` 200
DECIDE `small check` IS `is small` 2
